From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a page that hides the device's details reads it a
 little off

Brave's farbling: a page in a profile that hides the device's details
reads its canvas pictures and pixels, its rendered and analyzed audio and
its processor count a little off, the same way for its site all session.
The browser sends each frame its seed before it commits;
domicile::DeviceDetailsAgent, which ChromeContentRendererClient::
RenderFrameCreated gives every frame, hands it to the new document's
window (WebLocalFrame::SetDomicileDeviceDetailsSeed), and core/frame/
domicile_device_details.h farbles with it where a page reads each:
NavigatorBase::hardwareConcurrency, HTMLCanvasElement's toDataURL and
toBlob, BaseRenderingContext2D::getImageData, OfflineAudioContext's
rendered buffer and AnalyserNode's float data.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`.
